From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi: connection point of the voice events for automation clients

sapi: connection point of the voice events for automation clients

ISpeechVoice's IConnectionPointContainer methods were FIXME stubs.

- FindConnectionPoint answers _ISpeechVoiceEvents (CONNECT_E_NOCONNECTION for
  any other IID) and EnumConnectionPoints enumerates that one connection
  point (Next, Skip, Reset, Clone). The connection point has Advise (the
  sink must offer the events dispinterface or IDispatch,
  CONNECT_E_CANNOTCONNECT otherwise), Unadvise (CONNECT_E_NOCONNECTION for an
  unknown cookie), EnumConnections and the connection point container.
- The events of the voice (stream start and end, word, sentence, bookmark,
  phoneme, viseme, audio level and voice change) that are of interest are
  delivered to the sinks. They are posted to a message window of the thread
  that made the voice and invoked from there, which is what clients of
  automation expect (the thread has to run its message loop, as with the
  native SAPI).

